<!-- Parity fixture, hand-written for ProjectCraft's tests from Microsoft's published MSPDI schema
     documentation (learn.microsoft.com/office-project/xml-data-interchange). An invented plan:
     the tasks and dates are made up. No Microsoft file was used.

     What it exercises: the things ProjectCraft converts on import, each on a branch of its own so
     that one conversion's date difference doesn't run on into the next task: an elapsed duration,
     an elapsed lag, a percent lag, As Late As Possible, a task calendar, a constraint at a time of
     day other than the day's start, and an elapsed leveling delay.

     Each task's Start and Finish are written as Microsoft Project would work them out by its
     published scheduling rules, worked by hand. The project calendar: Monday to Friday 08:00 to
     12:00 and 13:00 to 17:00, a day is 8 hours; the Weekends base calendar works Saturdays and
     Sundays at the same times and no weekdays. Elapsed time runs round the clock, every day.

      1 Lift the old trees, 3d: Mon 5 to Wed 7 Oct 2026, 17:00.
      2 Soak the rootstock, 2ed (48 hours round the clock) from Mon 5 Oct 08:00: to Wed 7 Oct
        08:00. 5 Oct to 7 Oct.
      3 Dig planting pits, 2d, FS from 1 with a 3ed lag: 7 Oct 17:00 plus 72 hours is Sat 10 Oct
        17:00, so it starts Mon 12 Oct 08:00: 12 to 13 Oct.
      4 Stake the trees, 1d, FS from 1 with a 50% lag (half of 1's 3d, 12 working hours): Thu 8
        and Fri 9 Oct morning, so it starts Fri 9 Oct 13:00 and finishes Mon 12 Oct 12:00.
      6 Label the rows, 1d, FS from 4 and 5: Mon 12 Oct 13:00 to Tue 13 Oct 12:00.
      8 Mulch the rows, 1d, Start No Earlier Than Wed 14 Oct 13:00: to Thu 15 Oct 12:00, the
        project's finish.
      5 Order the labels, 1d, As Late As Possible, FS to 6: 6 may finish as late as the project's
        finish, 15 Oct 12:00, so start as late as Wed 14 Oct 13:00; 5 then finishes Wed 14 Oct
        12:00 and starts Tue 13 Oct 13:00.
      7 Weekend watering, 2d on the Weekends task calendar, FS from 1: Sat 10 and Sun 11 Oct.
      9 Prune the hedges, 1d, Start No Earlier Than Fri 9 Oct 08:00 and a leveling delay of 2ed:
        Fri 9 Oct 08:00 plus 48 hours is Sun 11 Oct 08:00, so it starts Mon 12 Oct 08:00, and
        finishes 12 Oct 17:00. -->
